# Conformance probe pack for the field options of spec 0.6 on the `bits` wire,
# most-significant-bit-first. Public. No kinds. One byte per word, so a locator
# is `0:<bit offset>:<len>`. Exercises `swap` (16 and 32 bits: little-endian
# fields in an `msb` pack), `trim`, `optional`, `const`, a value table from a
# wire integer to a model string, and `typemap` on the bits wire (ruling 18 of
# 0.5). Decode needs 12 bytes; encode writes 22.
format     conformance-rules-bits
version    0.6.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       track
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
bit_order  msb
const  0:0:8  90                                        # byte 0: 0x5a
field  time_ms      0:8:16    uint  swap                # bytes 1 to 2, little-endian
field  lat          0:24:32   sscale:1/10000000  swap   # bytes 3 to 6, little-endian
field  track.class  0:56:8    uint  via class           # byte 7
field  type         0:64:32   ascii                     # bytes 8 to 11, through the typemap
field  callsign     0:96:48   ascii  trim  optional     # bytes 12 to 17
field  ce           0:144:32  f32  optional  swap       # bytes 18 to 21, little-endian single
typemap FRND a-f-G
map    class  1  uas
map    class  2  bird
